{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XvZN5bAXyB6nSF79V2u9QB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '完全放弃selective verification contribution。转型为pure training methodology\n2\t  paper: ''Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and\n3\t  How to Fix It''。核心Figure是h-sweep + mechanism visualization。需要极细粒度h-sweep、多seed统计、与RAGEN的explicit对比来补偿绝对性能不impressive的弱点。Paper\n4\t  story变为：(1)揭示failure mode, (2)mechanistic explanation, (3)提出fix并验证。不降venue但需要更深analysis\n5\t  depth。'\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n8\t  plan_id: plan_002\n9\t  description: Sweep h={1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full} on same GRPO config. Paper核心Figure。\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    h1_success_rate: 0.0\n12\t    h2_success_rate: 2.0\n13\t    h3_success_rate: 4.5\n14\t    h5_success_rate: 8.0\n15\t    h8_success_rate: 14.0\n16\t    h10_success_rate: 18.0\n17\t    h15_success_rate: 22.0\n18\t    h20_success_rate: 24.0\n19\t    h_full_success_rate: 25.0\n20\t    cliff_threshold_h: 5\n21\t    h1_collapse_rate: 1.0\n22\t    h2_collapse_rate: 0.85\n23\t    h5_action_is_valid: 72.0\n24\t    h10_action_is_valid: 82.0\n25\t    h_full_action_is_valid: 88.0\n26\t    convergence_speed_h10_steps: 15\n27\t    convergence_speed_h_full_steps: 8\n28\t  result_rationale: 在worst档位下，h-sweep仍能展示episode-level vs step-independent的gap，但曲线形态偏向gradual\n29\t    degradation而非sharp cliff。h=5以下gamma^(T-h)衰减到<1%导致几乎无学习信号，但h=10到h=full之间差距不大（18%→25%），削弱了'episode-level\n30\t    is critical'的论证力度——reviewer会argue h=10 already sufficient。绝对性能ceiling在25%使得整条曲线都不impressive。cliff在h=5左右，比hypothesis的h=10低，意味着credit\n31\t    assignment threshold比预期更宽松，但也说明即便给了足够context（h≥10），1.7B model的能力ceiling也只有20-25%。\n32\t  tables:\n33\t  - name: 'Table 1: h-sweep results'\n34\t    columns:\n35\t    - h\n36\t    - success_rate(%)\n37\t    - action_is_valid(%)\n38\t    - convergence_step\n39\t    - effective_discount_gamma^(T-h)_mean\n40\t    rows:\n41\t    - - 1\n42\t      - 0.0\n43\t      - 45.0\n44\t      - N/A (collapse)\n45\t      - 0.0001\n46\t    - - 2\n47\t      - 2.0\n48\t      - 58.0\n49\t      - N/A (near-collapse)\n50\t      - 0.0008\n51\t    - - 3\n52\t      - 4.5\n53\t      - 65.0\n54\t      - 20\n55\t      - 0.005\n56\t    - - 5\n57\t      - 8.0\n58\t      - 72.0\n59\t      - 15\n60\t      - 0.03\n61\t    - - 8\n62\t      - 14.0\n63\t      - 79.0\n64\t      - 12\n65\t      - 0.12\n66\t    - - 10\n67\t      - 18.0\n68\t      - 82.0\n69\t      - 12\n70\t      - 0.22\n71\t    - - 15\n72\t      - 22.0\n73\t      - 85.0\n74\t      - 10\n75\t      - 0.48\n76\t    - - 20\n77\t      - 24.0\n78\t      - 87.0\n79\t      - 8\n80\t      - 0.67\n81\t    - - full\n82\t      - 25.0\n83\t      - 88.0\n84\t      - 8\n85\t      - 1.0\n86\t  figures_description:\n87\t  - 'Figure 2a: x=h value (log scale), y=success rate. 呈S-curve但slope较gentle。h<5区域flat\n88\t    near zero, h=5-10区域linear rise, h>10区域saturate at ~25%。Error bars from single\n89\t    seed较大。'\n90\t  - 'Figure 2b: x=effective discount gamma^(T-h), y=success rate. Near-linear relationship，但R²约0.85（非perfect\n91\t    fit）表明discount不是唯一因素。'\n92\t  analysis: h-sweep是worst档下paper最有价值的contribution。虽然绝对性能低，但趋势清晰：step-independent（h=1-2）catastrophically\n93\t    fails，episode-level（h=full）works。问题在于h=10已达full性能的72%（18/25），reviewer会argue full\n94\t    episode context非必要。Defense需要：(1)强调h=10在更长episode task上可能不够，(2)展示h=full的convergence\n95\t    speed优势，(3)argue 'full是最简方案，无需tune h'。Single seed数据使得intermediate h values的ordering可能有noise。\n96\t- name: Multi-seed replication (3 seeds)\n97\t  plan_id: plan_003\n98\t  description: 2 additional seeds for episode-level config. Report mean ± std。\n99\t  expected_results:\n100\t    seed1_success_rate: 25.0\n101\t    seed2_success_rate: 18.0\n102\t    seed3_success_rate: 30.0\n103\t    mean_success_rate: 24.3\n104\t    std_success_rate: 6.0\n105\t    seed1_convergence_step: 8\n106\t    seed2_convergence_step: 15\n107\t    seed3_convergence_step: 6\n108\t    seed1_action_is_valid: 88.0\n109\t    seed2_action_is_valid: 82.0\n110\t    seed3_action_is_valid: 90.0\n111\t    mean_action_is_valid: 86.7\n112\t    std_action_is_valid: 4.2\n113\t  result_rationale: Worst档定义multi-seed std>8pp，但我预测实际std在6-9pp范围——足以让reviewer质疑但不至于完全破坏结论。三个seed中一个会表现较差（18%），一个中等（25%，复现原始结果），一个稍好（30%）。这个variance部分来自ALFWorld\n114\t    task sampling的随机性（val set只有16 episodes），部分来自GRPO的inherent instability（高grad_norm,\n115\t    KL spikes在不同seed上timing不同）。1.7B模型的parameter space小，不同random init导致loss landscape上收敛到不同local\n116\t    optima。Mean 24.3%仍远超step-independent baseline（0-6%），但confidence interval宽。\n117\t  tables:\n118\t  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level results'\n119\t    columns:\n120\t    - Seed\n121\t    - Success Rate(%)\n122\t    - Action Valid(%)\n123\t    - Convergence Step\n124\t    - Final KL\n125\t    rows:\n126\t    - - 42\n127\t      - 25.0\n128\t      - 88.0\n129\t      - 8\n130\t      - 0.048\n131\t    - - 123\n132\t      - 18.0\n133\t      - 82.0\n134\t      - 15\n135\t      - 0.092\n136\t    - - 7\n137\t      - 30.0\n138\t      - 90.0\n139\t      - 6\n140\t      - 0.035\n141\t    - - Mean±Std\n142\t      - 24.3±6.0\n143\t      - 86.7±4.2\n144\t      - 9.7±4.7\n145\t      - 0.058±0.030\n146\t  figures_description:\n147\t  - 'Figure: Training curves (success rate vs step) for 3 seeds with shaded std band.\n148\t    Band很宽，尤其在step 5-15区间。Seed 123明显延迟收敛。'\n149\t  analysis: Std=6pp略好于worst档定义的8-12pp下界，但仍然problematic。N=3 seeds给出的confidence interval很宽（24.3±6.0意味着95%\n150\t    CI约为[12, 37]），reviewer会正确指出这不够。理想需要5+ seeds但GPU budget不允许。Defense策略：(1)承认limitation，(2)强调所有seeds都远超step-independent\n151\t    baseline 0%，(3)variance主要在收敛speed而非final direction。\n152\t- name: Credit assignment mechanism analysis (paper Figure 2)\n153\t  plan_id: plan_004\n154\t  description: 计算并可视化gamma^(T-h) effective discount, gradient signal strength, episode\n155\t    length correlation。\n156\t  expected_results:\n157\t    gamma_value_used: 0.99\n158\t    mean_episode_length_T: 48\n159\t    gamma_T_minus_1: 0.0061\n160\t    gamma_T_minus_2: 0.0062\n161\t    gamma_T_minus_5: 0.0065\n162\t    gamma_T_minus_10: 0.0068\n163\t    gamma_T_minus_20: 0.0075\n164\t    gamma_T_minus_full: 1.0\n165\t    gradient_signal_h1_relative: 0.006\n166\t    gradient_signal_h5_relative: 0.03\n167\t    gradient_signal_h10_relative: 0.22\n168\t    gradient_signal_full_relative: 1.0\n169\t    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.35\n170\t    long_episode_success_drop_under_h5: 95\n171\t  result_rationale: Mechanistic analysis本身是deterministic计算（给定gamma和episode length分布），不受worst档位的performance\n172\t    ceiling影响。ALFWorld平均episode length~48 steps，所以gamma^47≈0.006（h=1时first action的discount）。这个数学事实不变。但worst档下的complication是：即使h=full（gradient\n173\t    signal=1.0），模型也只达25%——说明gradient signal是necessary但非sufficient condition。Reviewer会argue：'你解决了gradient\n174\t    signal问题，但模型仍然不行，说明bottleneck在elsewhere'。需要explicitly address这一点：承认model capacity是另一个bottleneck，但credit\n175\t    assignment是第一个需解决的。\n176\t  tables:\n177\t  - name: 'Table 3: Effective discount factor analysis'\n178\t    columns:\n179\t    - h\n180\t    - Mean gamma^(T-h)\n181\t    - Relative Gradient Signal\n182\t    - Observed Success(%)\n183\t    rows:\n184\t    - - 1\n185\t      - 0.006\n186\t      - 0.6%\n187\t      - 0.0\n188\t    - - 2\n189\t      - 0.012\n190\t      - 1.2%\n191\t      - 2.0\n192\t    - - 5\n193\t      - 0.03\n194\t      - 3.0%\n195\t      - 8.0\n196\t    - - 10\n197\t      - 0.22\n198\t      - 22%\n199\t      - 18.0\n200\t    - - 20\n201\t      - 0.67\n202\t      - 67%\n203\t      - 24.0\n204\t    - - full\n205\t      - 1.0\n206\t      - 100%\n207\t      - 25.0\n208\t  figures_description:\n209\t  - 'Figure 2 (paper核心): 双y轴图。Left y=effective gradient signal (log scale), Right\n210\t    y=observed success rate. x=h value. 两条曲线形态高度相关但非identical，展示gradient signal是necessary\n211\t    condition。Annotation标注''failure zone'' (h<5, signal<3%), ''transition zone'' (h=5-10),\n212\t    ''saturation zone'' (h>10, 性能plateau at model capacity ceiling)。'\n213\t  - 'Figure 2b: Episode length histogram colored by success/failure. 长episode（>40\n214\t    steps）在h<10时success接近0，h=full时仍有部分成功。'\n215\t  analysis: 这是worst档下最强的contribution piece。数学关系清晰，可视化compelling。关键insight：在RAGEN等现有工作中，默认h=1（step-independent），对应gradient\n216\t    signal仅0.6%——解释了为什么这些方法在long-horizon tasks上struggle。但需要小心措辞：不能overclaim 'episode-level\n217\t    solves multi-turn RL'（因为25%不算solved），只能claim 'episode-level is necessary first\n218\t    step, removing a fundamental training bottleneck'。\n219\t- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n220\t  plan_id: plan_005\n221\t  description: 从exp029 checkpoints收集action-change统计：confirmatory rate, correlation\n222\t    with success, per-task breakdown。\n223\t  expected_results:\n224\t    total_verification_episodes: 48\n225\t    action_change_rate: 0.35\n226\t    confirmatory_rate: 0.65\n227\t    action_change_success_correlation_r: 0.15\n228\t    action_change_success_correlation_p: 0.18\n229\t    per_task_confirmatory_rate_put: 0.72\n230\t    per_task_confirmatory_rate_clean: 0.6\n231\t    per_task_confirmatory_rate_heat: 0.55\n232\t    per_task_confirmatory_rate_cool: 0.58\n233\t    per_task_confirmatory_rate_examine: 0.7\n234\t    action_change_leads_to_success_rate: 0.22\n235\t    no_change_leads_to_success_rate: 0.18\n236\t  result_rationale: 在worst档下，episode-level model只有25% success rate，导致action-change统计的样本量极小且noisy。Confirmatory\n237\t    rate 65%落在worst档定义的50-70%范围内，但correlation with success仅r=0.15（p=0.18, not significant）。这是因为：(1)成功episodes太少（~12/48），统计power不足；(2)25%的模型经常在错误轨道上，verification后的action\n238\t    change可能是从一个错误action换到另一个错误action，而非corrective。Action change→success rate (22%)\n239\t    vs no change→success rate (18%)的delta仅4pp，远不够支撑'action change is informative signal'的claim。这直接explains为什么在worst档下必须放弃selective\n240\t    verification story。\n241\t  tables:\n242\t  - name: 'Table: Action-change statistics'\n243\t    columns:\n244\t    - Metric\n245\t    - Value\n246\t    - 95% CI\n247\t    rows:\n248\t    - - Confirmatory rate (no action change)\n249\t      - 65%\n250\t      - '[52%, 78%]'\n251\t    - - Action change rate\n252\t      - 35%\n253\t      - '[22%, 48%]'\n254\t    - - Correlation (action_change, success)\n255\t      - r=0.15\n256\t      - p=0.18\n257\t    - - Success | action_change\n258\t      - 22%\n259\t      - '[10%, 34%]'\n260\t    - - Success | no_change\n261\t      - 18%\n262\t      - '[8%, 28%]'\n263\t  figures_description:\n264\t  - 'Bar chart: per-task confirmatory rate. All tasks >55% confirmatory. Wide error\n265\t    bars due to small N per task type.'\n266\t  analysis: 统计结果不支持action-change作为meaningful reward signal。Correlation not significant，delta\n267\t    too small，CI too wide。这组数据是worst档叙事转向的empirical justification：不是我们选择不做selective\n268\t    verification，而是数据显示在当前performance level下selective verification lacks statistical\n269\t    grounding。Paper中可以brief mention作为'future work when base agent is stronger'。\n270\t- name: Selective verification implementation\n271\t  plan_id: plan_006\n272\t  description: 实现binary verify/skip decision。Code-only, no GPU。\n273\t  expected_results:\n274\t    implementation_status: completed\n275\t    code_lines_added: 350\n276\t    integration_test_pass: true\n277\t    note: implementation ready but not deployed for training due to plan_005 results\n278\t  result_rationale: Implementation本身是engineering work，不受worst档影响。代码可以完成，但基于plan_005的统计结果（action-change\n279\t    correlation not significant），decision是不proceed to training。代码保留为future work artifact。\n280\t  tables: []\n281\t  figures_description: []\n282\t  analysis: 在worst档叙事下，这个实验stop at implementation。Paper中不报告selective verification\n283\t    training results，而是在discussion section brief mention implementation exists but\n284\t    'requires stronger base agent to provide meaningful training signal'。\n285\t- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n286\t  plan_id: plan_007\n287\t  description: Train selective verification policy via episode-level GRPO。在worst档下执行但预期效果不佳。\n288\t  expected_results:\n289\t    training_status: completed_but_ineffective\n290\t    final_success_rate: 18.0\n291\t    always_on_baseline_success: 25.0\n292\t    success_delta_vs_always_on: -7.0\n293\t    verification_rate_reduction: 12.0\n294\t    cost_reduction_pct: 8.0\n295\t    training_stability: unstable\n296\t    convergence_step: no clear convergence\n297\t    reward_signal_noise: high\n298\t  result_rationale: Worst档定义selective_verification_rate_reduction在0-15%，selective_vs_always_on_success_delta在8-15pp。模型从25%\n299\t    base开始，加入verify/skip decision后引入额外exploration space，但base performance本身就marginal。Agent在只有25%\n300\t    success的情况下，缺乏足够的positive reward signal来学习WHEN to verify——大部分trajectory都是failure，无论verify还是skip。结果是verification\n301\t    rate仅下降12%（几乎always verify因为policy没学到有用的skip pattern），且success下降7pp（从25%到18%）因为额外decision\n302\t    point增加了policy complexity。这不构成meaningful contribution。\n303\t  tables:\n304\t  - name: 'Table: B-IAVR training outcome'\n305\t    columns:\n306\t    - Config\n307\t    - Success(%)\n308\t    - Verify Rate(%)\n309\t    - Cost Reduction(%)\n310\t    rows:\n311\t    - - Always-on (baseline)\n312\t      - 25.0\n313\t      - 100\n314\t      - 0\n315\t    - - B-IAVR (trained)\n316\t      - 18.0\n317\t      - 88\n318\t      - 8\n319\t    - - Delta\n320\t      - -7.0\n321\t      - -12\n322\t      - '+8'\n323\t  figures_description:\n324\t  - Training curve extremely noisy, no clear trend in verification rate reduction\n325\t    over steps.\n326\t  analysis: 结果confirms worst档prediction：selective verification在base agent只有25%时无法有意义地训练。-7pp\n327\t    success drop换取仅8% cost reduction，Pareto-dominated by always-on。Paper中不报告此结果，或仅作为negative\n328\t    result brief mention to motivate 'stronger base agent needed'。\n329\t- name: Selective verification full comparison\n330\t  plan_id: plan_008\n331\t  description: Compare always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold。\n332\t  expected_results:\n333\t    always_on_success: 25.0\n334\t    always_on_verify_rate: 100\n335\t    biavr_success: 18.0\n336\t    biavr_verify_rate: 88\n337\t    no_verify_success: 15.0\n338\t    no_verify_verify_rate: 0\n339\t    random_p50_success: 20.0\n340\t    random_p50_verify_rate: 50\n341\t    confidence_threshold_success: 21.0\n342\t    confidence_threshold_verify_rate: 65\n343\t  result_rationale: 在25% ceiling下，所有selective methods都worse than always-on。Random-p=0.5\n344\t    (20%) actually competitive with trained B-IAVR (18%)——trained policy没有学到比random更好的策略，这是devastating\n345\t    negative result。Confidence-threshold (21%) slightly better因为它是heuristic rule而非learned，less\n346\t    prone to policy degradation。整个comparison suite展示：在low-performance regime下，verification的选择性本身不是bottleneck，base\n347\t    capability才是。\n348\t  tables:\n349\t  - name: 'Table: Full comparison (NOT included in worst-tier paper)'\n350\t    columns:\n351\t    - Method\n352\t    - Success(%)\n353\t    - Verify Rate(%)\n354\t    - Tokens/Episode\n355\t    - Cost Reduction(%)\n356\t    rows:\n357\t    - - Always-on\n358\t      - 25.0\n359\t      - 100\n360\t      - 4800\n361\t      - 0\n362\t    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n363\t      - 18.0\n364\t      - 88\n365\t      - 4420\n366\t      - 8\n367\t    - - No-verify\n368\t      - 15.0\n369\t      - 0\n370\t      - 2400\n371\t      - 50\n372\t    - - Random-p=0.5\n373\t      - 20.0\n374\t      - 50\n375\t      - 3600\n376\t      - 25\n377\t    - - Confidence-threshold\n378\t      - 21.0\n379\t      - 65\n380\t      - 3900\n381\t      - 19\n382\t  figures_description:\n383\t  - 'Pareto plot (x=cost, y=success): B-IAVR dominated by random-p and confidence-threshold.\n384\t    Only always-on achieves max success.'\n385\t  analysis: 'This entire comparison suite becomes ''data we collected but don''t include\n386\t    in paper''。B-IAVR被simpler baselines dominate是fatal for selective verification\n387\t    claim。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这组数据的唯一价值是supporting the narrative ''future\n388\t    work: once episode-level training achieves higher ceiling, selective verification\n389\t    becomes viable''。'\n390\t- name: No-verify ablation\n391\t  plan_id: plan_009\n392\t  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。Lower bound实验。\n393\t  expected_results:\n394\t    success_rate: 15.0\n395\t    action_is_valid: 78.0\n396\t    delta_vs_always_on: -10.0\n397\t    mean_episode_length: 38\n398\t    convergence_step: 10\n399\t  result_rationale: 移除verification后，agent失去每步的self-correction机会。从25%降到15%，delta=10pp。这在worst档下actually是有用的数据点——证明verification本身有10pp价值。但这个delta不够dramatic来支撑'selective\n400\t    verification is the key innovation'的story。在pure methodology paper中可以brief report作为：'verification\n401\t    contributes +10pp, confirming its utility, but our focus is on the training methodology\n402\t    that enables ANY multi-turn RL to work'。\n403\t  tables:\n404\t  - name: 'Table: Verification value'\n405\t    columns:\n406\t    - Config\n407\t    - Success(%)\n408\t    - Action Valid(%)\n409\t    - Avg Steps\n410\t    rows:\n411\t    - - Episode-level + verification\n412\t      - 25.0\n413\t      - 88.0\n414\t      - 48\n415\t    - - Episode-level, no verification\n416\t      - 15.0\n417\t      - 78.0\n418\t      - 38\n419\t    - - Step-independent + verification\n420\t      - 0.0\n421\t      - 65.0\n422\t      - 50\n423\t  figures_description: []\n424\t  analysis: '三行对比table实际很有说服力：step-independent完全fails无论有无verification，episode-level\n425\t    without verification仍有15%。Message: training methodology是前提条件，verification是锦上添花。这fit\n426\t    worst档pure methodology paper的narrative。'\n427\t- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n428\t  plan_id: plan_010\n429\t  description: Stratify action-change correlation by policy entropy, test partial\n430\t    correlation。\n431\t  expected_results:\n432\t    overall_correlation_r: 0.15\n433\t    overall_p: 0.18\n434\t    low_entropy_stratum_r: 0.08\n435\t    low_entropy_stratum_p: 0.55\n436\t    high_entropy_stratum_r: 0.2\n437\t    high_entropy_stratum_p: 0.22\n438\t    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.12\n439\t    partial_correlation_p: 0.28\n440\t    n_episodes_per_stratum: 24\n441\t  result_rationale: 在worst档25% success下，整体correlation已not significant (r=0.15, p=0.18)。Stratify\n442\t    by entropy后每层只有~24 episodes，statistical power进一步削弱。Low entropy stratum（policy\n443\t    confident）中action-change很少发生（agent已committed to action），correlation near zero。High\n444\t    entropy stratum中有more action-change但也more randomness，correlation略高但仍not significant。Partial\n445\t    correlation r=0.12 (p=0.28)完全不支持'action-change is signal not noise'的claim。根本原因：样本量太小\n446\t    + base performance太低导致signal-to-noise ratio极差。\n447\t  tables: []\n448\t  figures_description: []\n449\t  analysis: '在worst档下这组分析的结论是negative：无法reject null hypothesis (action-change = noise)。Paper中不report，或在appendix作为''limitation:\n450\t    at current performance level, insufficient statistical power to establish action-change\n451\t    as reliable signal''。'\n452\t- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n453\t  plan_id: plan_011\n454\t  description: Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered. Compare success。\n455\t  expected_results:\n456\t    verification_triggered_success: 22.0\n457\t    random_change_success: 16.0\n458\t    no_change_baseline_success: 18.0\n459\t    delta_triggered_vs_random: 6.0\n460\t    delta_triggered_vs_random_p: 0.25\n461\t    n_episodes: 48\n462\t  result_rationale: Verification-triggered changes (22%) vs random changes (16%) shows\n463\t    6pp gap，方向正确但p=0.25 not significant。N=48 episodes不够detect这个effect size。No-change\n464\t    baseline (18%)介于两者之间，使得interpretation模糊：triggered changes可能beneficial，但也可能just\n465\t    noise given wide CIs。在25% performance regime下，即使verification IS informative，effect\n466\t    size太小to detect reliably。另一个confounder：random changes有时accidentally correct（16%\n467\t    vs no-change 18%只差2pp），suggesting verification的causal contribution marginal。\n468\t  tables:\n469\t  - name: 'Table: Causal intervention (insufficient power)'\n470\t    columns:\n471\t    - Condition\n472\t    - Success(%)\n473\t    - N\n474\t    - 95% CI\n475\t    rows:\n476\t    - - Verification-triggered change\n477\t      - 22.0\n478\t      - 48\n479\t      - '[11%, 33%]'\n480\t    - - Random change (same rate)\n481\t      - 16.0\n482\t      - 48\n483\t      - '[6%, 26%]'\n484\t    - - No change control\n485\t      - 18.0\n486\t      - 48\n487\t      - '[8%, 28%]'\n488\t  figures_description: []\n489\t  analysis: CIs完全overlap。Experiment was run but results inconclusive。在pure methodology\n490\t    paper中不report。File under 'more data needed at higher performance level'。\n491\t- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n492\t  plan_id: plan_012\n493\t  description: 'Train B-IAVR with different reward signals: action-change, random,\n494\t    confidence-based。'\n495\t  expected_results:\n496\t    action_change_reward_success: 18.0\n497\t    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 88\n498\t    random_reward_success: 17.0\n499\t    random_reward_verify_rate: 82\n500\t    confidence_reward_success: 19.0\n501\t    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 85\n502\t    all_configs_worse_than_always_on: true\n503\t    best_reward_signal: confidence (marginal)\n504\t  result_rationale: 所有reward signals在25% base下都无法学到meaningful selective policy。Action-change\n505\t    reward (18%, verify 88%) vs random reward (17%, verify 82%)的差距仅1pp success——action-change没有demonstrable\n506\t    advantage over random。Confidence-based reward margionally better (19%) because它at\n507\t    least correlates with model's own uncertainty（哪怕calibration差）。但关键point：所有trained\n508\t    selective policies都worse than always-on (25%)。Reward signal choice irrelevant\n509\t    when base performance insufficient to generate learning signal。192 GPU hours换来的结论是'all\n510\t    approaches fail equally in low-performance regime'。\n511\t  tables:\n512\t  - name: 'Table: Reward ablation (NOT in paper)'\n513\t    columns:\n514\t    - Reward Signal\n515\t    - Success(%)\n516\t    - Verify Rate(%)\n517\t    - vs Always-on Delta\n518\t    rows:\n519\t    - - Action-change (ours)\n520\t      - 18.0\n521\t      - 88\n522\t      - -7\n523\t    - - Random trigger\n524\t      - 17.0\n525\t      - 82\n526\t      - -8\n527\t    - - Confidence-based\n528\t      - 19.0\n529\t      - 85\n530\t      - -6\n531\t    - - Always-on (no selection)\n532\t      - 25.0\n533\t      - 100\n534\t      - 0\n535\t  figures_description: []\n536\t  analysis: 192 GPU hours for a negative result。在worst档下，建议NOT run此实验——plan_007的negative\n537\t    result已sufficient to abandon selective verification direction。Save GPU budget\n538\t    for more h-sweep seeds or ScienceWorld transfer。\n539\t- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n540\t  plan_id: plan_013\n541\t  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR。\n542\t  expected_results:\n543\t    ares_success: 20.0\n544\t    ares_verify_rate: 60\n545\t    ares_cost_reduction: 30\n546\t    biavr_success: 18.0\n547\t    biavr_verify_rate: 88\n548\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 8\n549\t    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n550\t  result_rationale: ARES使用SFT（supervised从expert demonstrations学）which is more data-efficient\n551\t    than RL in low-performance regime。SFT router可以直接学human-pattern的'when to verify'而不依赖agent自身的exploration。预测ARES\n552\t    achieves 20% success at 60% verify rate，Pareto-dominating B-IAVR (18% at 88% verify\n553\t    rate)。这是because SFT不需要agent自己产生positive signal——它从expert data中学。Devastating for\n554\t    our RL-based approach，但irrelevant for worst档paper because we abandon selective\n555\t    verification entirely。\n556\t  tables:\n557\t  - name: 'Table: ARES comparison (NOT in paper)'\n558\t    columns:\n559\t    - Method\n560\t    - Success(%)\n561\t    - Verify Rate(%)\n562\t    - Cost Red.(%)\n563\t    rows:\n564\t    - - Always-on\n565\t      - 25.0\n566\t      - 100\n567\t      - 0\n568\t    - - ARES (SFT router)\n569\t      - 20.0\n570\t      - 60\n571\t      - 30\n572\t    - - B-IAVR (ours, RL)\n573\t      - 18.0\n574\t      - 88\n575\t      - 8\n576\t  figures_description: []\n577\t  analysis: ARES dominates B-IAVR on Pareto frontier。但在worst档pure methodology paper中，这个comparison不needed也不helpful。如果include，只会invite\n578\t    reviewer质疑'why not just use SFT'。建议NOT run，节省24 GPU hours。\n579\t- name: ScienceWorld transfer (episode-level advantage)\n580\t  plan_id: plan_014\n581\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。Second environment\n582\t    for generalization。\n583\t  expected_results:\n584\t    episode_level_success: 15.0\n585\t    step_independent_success: 2.0\n586\t    episode_level_action_is_valid: 75.0\n587\t    step_independent_action_is_valid: 55.0\n588\t    episode_level_convergence_step: 12\n589\t    step_independent_collapse_step: 4\n590\t    mean_episode_length_scienceworld: 35\n591\t  result_rationale: ScienceWorld比ALFWorld更难（state space更大，natural language更复杂），1.7B\n592\t    model的absolute performance会更低。Episode-level仍展示优势（15% vs 2%），倍率~7.5x（高于ALFWorld的~4x因为ScienceWorld的longer\n593\t    episodes使credit assignment问题更severe）。Step-independent在step 4 collapse（与ALFWorld\n594\t    pattern一致）。绝对数字15%不impressive，但cross-environment consistency是powerful evidence\n595\t    for the mechanism。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这是ADDRESS single-environment\n596\t    concern的关键实验。\n597\t  tables:\n598\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-environment validation'\n599\t    columns:\n600\t    - Environment\n601\t    - Episode-Level(%)\n602\t    - Step-Independent(%)\n603\t    - Ratio\n604\t    - Mean Episode Length\n605\t    rows:\n606\t    - - ALFWorld\n607\t      - 25.0\n608\t      - 0.0\n609\t      - ∞ (0→25)\n610\t      - 48\n611\t    - - ScienceWorld\n612\t      - 15.0\n613\t      - 2.0\n614\t      - 7.5x\n615\t      - 35\n616\t  figures_description:\n617\t  - 'Side-by-side training curves for both environments. Same pattern: step-independent\n618\t    collapses early, episode-level converges (albeit to low absolute value).'\n619\t  analysis: 'Cross-environment result是worst档paper的第二大contribution。Pattern consistent\n620\t    across environments strongly支持mechanistic explanation。Reviewer concern #2 (single\n621\t    env) addressed。72 GPU hours well-spent for worst档narrative。绝对值低但ratio large，且collapse\n622\t    pattern identical——这是methodology insight的generalization evidence。'\n623\t- name: 7B model scaling verification\n624\t  plan_id: plan_015\n625\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B。Address model size concern。\n626\t  expected_results:\n627\t    episode_level_7b_success: 38.0\n628\t    step_independent_7b_success: 5.0\n629\t    episode_level_7b_action_is_valid: 92.0\n630\t    step_independent_7b_collapse_step: 5\n631\t    episode_level_7b_convergence_step: 6\n632\t    delta_7b_vs_1_7b_episode_level: 13\n633\t  result_rationale: 7B model有更高的capability ceiling，episode-level可能达38%（接近40% threshold但仍在worst档范围内——worst档是关于1.7B的performance，7B\n634\t    naturally higher）。Step-independent 7B同样collapse at step 5 (5% max)，确认credit assignment问题is\n635\t    model-size independent。7B的38% vs 1.7B的25%（+13pp）部分validates 'model capacity is\n636\t    separate bottleneck' argument。但192 GPU hours + cloud rental成本高。在worst档下，如果budget\n637\t    tight，这是high-value但high-cost experiment。如果run，结果强力支持narrative：'episode-level advantage\n638\t    holds across scales; larger models achieve higher ceiling但step-independent依然fails\n639\t    regardless of scale'。\n640\t  tables:\n641\t  - name: 'Table: Model scaling'\n642\t    columns:\n643\t    - Model\n644\t    - Episode-Level(%)\n645\t    - Step-Independent(%)\n646\t    - Advantage\n647\t    rows:\n648\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n649\t      - 25.0\n650\t      - 0.0\n651\t      - +25pp\n652\t    - - Qwen3-7B\n653\t      - 38.0\n654\t      - 5.0\n655\t      - +33pp\n656\t  figures_description:\n657\t  - 'Bar chart: episode-level advantage grows with model size (from +25pp to +33pp),\n658\t    suggesting larger models benefit MORE from episode-level training (because they\n659\t    have more capacity to exploit the better gradient signal).'\n660\t  analysis: '如果budget允许，这是worst档paper最能silence reviewer的实验。7B result (38% vs 5%) is\n661\t    more impressive than 1.7B result (25% vs 0%)。Combined message: ''the training\n662\t    methodology enables the model capacity to be utilized; without it, even larger\n663\t    models fail''。论文可能需要重新定位：如果7B reaches 38%，接近40% threshold，paper的overall strength\n664\t    significantly improves even under worst-tier 1.7B results。'\n665\t- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n666\t  plan_id: plan_016\n667\t  description: Breakdown by ALFWorld task type. Shows within-environment diversity。\n668\t  expected_results:\n669\t    pick_success_episode_level: 30.0\n670\t    pick_success_step_independent: 0.0\n671\t    clean_success_episode_level: 20.0\n672\t    clean_success_step_independent: 0.0\n673\t    heat_success_episode_level: 25.0\n674\t    heat_success_step_independent: 0.0\n675\t    cool_success_episode_level: 35.0\n676\t    cool_success_step_independent: 5.0\n677\t    examine_success_episode_level: 10.0\n678\t    examine_success_step_independent: 0.0\n679\t    pick_two_success_episode_level: 5.0\n680\t    pick_two_success_step_independent: 0.0\n681\t    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.42\n682\t    short_task_advantage: cool/heat (fewer steps) have higher success\n683\t  result_rationale: '在worst档下，per-task breakdown reveals episode-level advantage is\n684\t    universal但magnitude varies by task complexity。Shorter tasks (cool: ~30 steps,\n685\t    heat: ~35 steps) reach higher success (35%, 25%) because credit assignment even\n686\t    under h=full works better when T is smaller (gamma^0=1 for last step matters more\n687\t    when T smaller)。Longer tasks (examine: ~50 steps, pick_two: ~55 steps) have lower\n688\t    success (10%, 5%) — model capacity ceiling hits harder when trajectory is longer。Correlation\n689\t    r=-0.42 between episode length and success confirms mechanistic explanation。Step-independent\n690\t    fails uniformly across all types (0-5%), confirming the training failure is systematic\n691\t    not task-specific。'\n692\t  tables:\n693\t  - name: 'Table: Per-task breakdown'\n694\t    columns:\n695\t    - Task Type\n696\t    - Avg Episode Length\n697\t    - Episode-Level(%)\n698\t    - Step-Independent(%)\n699\t    - N (val)\n700\t    rows:\n701\t    - - pick\n702\t      - 45\n703\t      - 30.0\n704\t      - 0.0\n705\t      - 4\n706\t    - - clean\n707\t      - 48\n708\t      - 20.0\n709\t      - 0.0\n710\t      - 3\n711\t    - - heat\n712\t      - 35\n713\t      - 25.0\n714\t      - 0.0\n715\t      - 3\n716\t    - - cool\n717\t      - 30\n718\t      - 35.0\n719\t      - 5.0\n720\t      - 3\n721\t    - - examine\n722\t      - 50\n723\t      - 10.0\n724\t      - 0.0\n725\t      - 2\n726\t    - - pick_two\n727\t      - 55\n728\t      - 5.0\n729\t      - 0.0\n730\t      - 1\n731\t  figures_description:\n732\t  - 'Scatter plot: x=mean episode length per task type, y=episode-level success rate.\n733\t    Negative correlation visible. Annotation: ''longer tasks → weaker signal even\n734\t    with full context (more steps to credit-assign across)''.'\n735\t  analysis: Small N per task type (1-4 episodes in val set) makes individual percentages\n736\t    unreliable，但overall trend (shorter tasks → higher success) supports mechanistic\n737\t    story。In worst档paper，include as supplementary analysis showing the method's advantage\n738\t    is consistent across task types despite varying magnitude。The length-success correlation\n739\t    adds another data point for the credit assignment narrative。\n740\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6de2f966-8909-4f3c-95c6-636800eb7308","uuid":"50b561bf-f393-4fcc-9301-9ba6b71424ef","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:26:43.943Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '完全放弃selective verification contribution。转型为pure training methodology\n  paper: ''Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Fails and\n  How to Fix It''。核心Figure是h-sweep + mechanism visualization。需要极细粒度h-sweep、多seed统计、与RAGEN的explicit对比来补偿绝对性能不impressive的弱点。Paper\n  story变为：(1)揭示failure mode, (2)mechanistic explanation, (3)提出fix并验证。不降venue但需要更深analysis\n  depth。'\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: Sweep h={1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full} on same GRPO config. Paper核心Figure。\n  expected_results:\n    h1_success_rate: 0.0\n    h2_success_rate: 2.0\n    h3_success_rate: 4.5\n    h5_success_rate: 8.0\n    h8_success_rate: 14.0\n    h10_success_rate: 18.0\n    h15_success_rate: 22.0\n    h20_success_rate: 24.0\n    h_full_success_rate: 25.0\n    cliff_threshold_h: 5\n    h1_collapse_rate: 1.0\n    h2_collapse_rate: 0.85\n    h5_action_is_valid: 72.0\n    h10_action_is_valid: 82.0\n    h_full_action_is_valid: 88.0\n    convergence_speed_h10_steps: 15\n    convergence_speed_h_full_steps: 8\n  result_rationale: 在worst档位下，h-sweep仍能展示episode-level vs step-independent的gap，但曲线形态偏向gradual\n    degradation而非sharp cliff。h=5以下gamma^(T-h)衰减到<1%导致几乎无学习信号，但h=10到h=full之间差距不大（18%→25%），削弱了'episode-level\n    is critical'的论证力度——reviewer会argue h=10 already sufficient。绝对性能ceiling在25%使得整条曲线都不impressive。cliff在h=5左右，比hypothesis的h=10低，意味着credit\n    assignment threshold比预期更宽松，但也说明即便给了足够context（h≥10），1.7B model的能力ceiling也只有20-25%。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: h-sweep results'\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - success_rate(%)\n    - action_is_valid(%)\n    - convergence_step\n    - effective_discount_gamma^(T-h)_mean\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.0\n      - 45.0\n      - N/A (collapse)\n      - 0.0001\n    - - 2\n      - 2.0\n      - 58.0\n      - N/A (near-collapse)\n      - 0.0008\n    - - 3\n      - 4.5\n      - 65.0\n      - 20\n      - 0.005\n    - - 5\n      - 8.0\n      - 72.0\n      - 15\n      - 0.03\n    - - 8\n      - 14.0\n      - 79.0\n      - 12\n      - 0.12\n    - - 10\n      - 18.0\n      - 82.0\n      - 12\n      - 0.22\n    - - 15\n      - 22.0\n      - 85.0\n      - 10\n      - 0.48\n    - - 20\n      - 24.0\n      - 87.0\n      - 8\n      - 0.67\n    - - full\n      - 25.0\n      - 88.0\n      - 8\n      - 1.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2a: x=h value (log scale), y=success rate. 呈S-curve但slope较gentle。h<5区域flat\n    near zero, h=5-10区域linear rise, h>10区域saturate at ~25%。Error bars from single\n    seed较大。'\n  - 'Figure 2b: x=effective discount gamma^(T-h), y=success rate. Near-linear relationship，但R²约0.85（非perfect\n    fit）表明discount不是唯一因素。'\n  analysis: h-sweep是worst档下paper最有价值的contribution。虽然绝对性能低，但趋势清晰：step-independent（h=1-2）catastrophically\n    fails，episode-level（h=full）works。问题在于h=10已达full性能的72%（18/25），reviewer会argue full\n    episode context非必要。Defense需要：(1)强调h=10在更长episode task上可能不够，(2)展示h=full的convergence\n    speed优势，(3)argue 'full是最简方案，无需tune h'。Single seed数据使得intermediate h values的ordering可能有noise。\n- name: Multi-seed replication (3 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 2 additional seeds for episode-level config. Report mean ± std。\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_success_rate: 25.0\n    seed2_success_rate: 18.0\n    seed3_success_rate: 30.0\n    mean_success_rate: 24.3\n    std_success_rate: 6.0\n    seed1_convergence_step: 8\n    seed2_convergence_step: 15\n    seed3_convergence_step: 6\n    seed1_action_is_valid: 88.0\n    seed2_action_is_valid: 82.0\n    seed3_action_is_valid: 90.0\n    mean_action_is_valid: 86.7\n    std_action_is_valid: 4.2\n  result_rationale: Worst档定义multi-seed std>8pp，但我预测实际std在6-9pp范围——足以让reviewer质疑但不至于完全破坏结论。三个seed中一个会表现较差（18%），一个中等（25%，复现原始结果），一个稍好（30%）。这个variance部分来自ALFWorld\n    task sampling的随机性（val set只有16 episodes），部分来自GRPO的inherent instability（高grad_norm,\n    KL spikes在不同seed上timing不同）。1.7B模型的parameter space小，不同random init导致loss landscape上收敛到不同local\n    optima。Mean 24.3%仍远超step-independent baseline（0-6%），但confidence interval宽。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 2: Multi-seed episode-level results'\n    columns:\n    - Seed\n    - Success Rate(%)\n    - Action Valid(%)\n    - Convergence Step\n    - Final KL\n    rows:\n    - - 42\n      - 25.0\n      - 88.0\n      - 8\n      - 0.048\n    - - 123\n      - 18.0\n      - 82.0\n      - 15\n      - 0.092\n    - - 7\n      - 30.0\n      - 90.0\n      - 6\n      - 0.035\n    - - Mean±Std\n      - 24.3±6.0\n      - 86.7±4.2\n      - 9.7±4.7\n      - 0.058±0.030\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Training curves (success rate vs step) for 3 seeds with shaded std band.\n    Band很宽，尤其在step 5-15区间。Seed 123明显延迟收敛。'\n  analysis: Std=6pp略好于worst档定义的8-12pp下界，但仍然problematic。N=3 seeds给出的confidence interval很宽（24.3±6.0意味着95%\n    CI约为[12, 37]），reviewer会正确指出这不够。理想需要5+ seeds但GPU budget不允许。Defense策略：(1)承认limitation，(2)强调所有seeds都远超step-independent\n    baseline 0%，(3)variance主要在收敛speed而非final direction。\n- name: Credit assignment mechanism analysis (paper Figure 2)\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: 计算并可视化gamma^(T-h) effective discount, gradient signal strength, episode\n    length correlation。\n  expected_results:\n    gamma_value_used: 0.99\n    mean_episode_length_T: 48\n    gamma_T_minus_1: 0.0061\n    gamma_T_minus_2: 0.0062\n    gamma_T_minus_5: 0.0065\n    gamma_T_minus_10: 0.0068\n    gamma_T_minus_20: 0.0075\n    gamma_T_minus_full: 1.0\n    gradient_signal_h1_relative: 0.006\n    gradient_signal_h5_relative: 0.03\n    gradient_signal_h10_relative: 0.22\n    gradient_signal_full_relative: 1.0\n    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.35\n    long_episode_success_drop_under_h5: 95\n  result_rationale: Mechanistic analysis本身是deterministic计算（给定gamma和episode length分布），不受worst档位的performance\n    ceiling影响。ALFWorld平均episode length~48 steps，所以gamma^47≈0.006（h=1时first action的discount）。这个数学事实不变。但worst档下的complication是：即使h=full（gradient\n    signal=1.0），模型也只达25%——说明gradient signal是necessary但非sufficient condition。Reviewer会argue：'你解决了gradient\n    signal问题，但模型仍然不行，说明bottleneck在elsewhere'。需要explicitly address这一点：承认model capacity是另一个bottleneck，但credit\n    assignment是第一个需解决的。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 3: Effective discount factor analysis'\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - Mean gamma^(T-h)\n    - Relative Gradient Signal\n    - Observed Success(%)\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.6%\n      - 0.0\n    - - 2\n      - 0.012\n      - 1.2%\n      - 2.0\n    - - 5\n      - 0.03\n      - 3.0%\n      - 8.0\n    - - 10\n      - 0.22\n      - 22%\n      - 18.0\n    - - 20\n      - 0.67\n      - 67%\n      - 24.0\n    - - full\n      - 1.0\n      - 100%\n      - 25.0\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2 (paper核心): 双y轴图。Left y=effective gradient signal (log scale), Right\n    y=observed success rate. x=h value. 两条曲线形态高度相关但非identical，展示gradient signal是necessary\n    condition。Annotation标注''failure zone'' (h<5, signal<3%), ''transition zone'' (h=5-10),\n    ''saturation zone'' (h>10, 性能plateau at model capacity ceiling)。'\n  - 'Figure 2b: Episode length histogram colored by success/failure. 长episode（>40\n    steps）在h<10时success接近0，h=full时仍有部分成功。'\n  analysis: 这是worst档下最强的contribution piece。数学关系清晰，可视化compelling。关键insight：在RAGEN等现有工作中，默认h=1（step-independent），对应gradient\n    signal仅0.6%——解释了为什么这些方法在long-horizon tasks上struggle。但需要小心措辞：不能overclaim 'episode-level\n    solves multi-turn RL'（因为25%不算solved），只能claim 'episode-level is necessary first\n    step, removing a fundamental training bottleneck'。\n- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: 从exp029 checkpoints收集action-change统计：confirmatory rate, correlation\n    with success, per-task breakdown。\n  expected_results:\n    total_verification_episodes: 48\n    action_change_rate: 0.35\n    confirmatory_rate: 0.65\n    action_change_success_correlation_r: 0.15\n    action_change_success_correlation_p: 0.18\n    per_task_confirmatory_rate_put: 0.72\n    per_task_confirmatory_rate_clean: 0.6\n    per_task_confirmatory_rate_heat: 0.55\n    per_task_confirmatory_rate_cool: 0.58\n    per_task_confirmatory_rate_examine: 0.7\n    action_change_leads_to_success_rate: 0.22\n    no_change_leads_to_success_rate: 0.18\n  result_rationale: 在worst档下，episode-level model只有25% success rate，导致action-change统计的样本量极小且noisy。Confirmatory\n    rate 65%落在worst档定义的50-70%范围内，但correlation with success仅r=0.15（p=0.18, not significant）。这是因为：(1)成功episodes太少（~12/48），统计power不足；(2)25%的模型经常在错误轨道上，verification后的action\n    change可能是从一个错误action换到另一个错误action，而非corrective。Action change→success rate (22%)\n    vs no change→success rate (18%)的delta仅4pp，远不够支撑'action change is informative signal'的claim。这直接explains为什么在worst档下必须放弃selective\n    verification story。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Action-change statistics'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Value\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - Confirmatory rate (no action change)\n      - 65%\n      - '[52%, 78%]'\n    - - Action change rate\n      - 35%\n      - '[22%, 48%]'\n    - - Correlation (action_change, success)\n      - r=0.15\n      - p=0.18\n    - - Success | action_change\n      - 22%\n      - '[10%, 34%]'\n    - - Success | no_change\n      - 18%\n      - '[8%, 28%]'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: per-task confirmatory rate. All tasks >55% confirmatory. Wide error\n    bars due to small N per task type.'\n  analysis: 统计结果不支持action-change作为meaningful reward signal。Correlation not significant，delta\n    too small，CI too wide。这组数据是worst档叙事转向的empirical justification：不是我们选择不做selective\n    verification，而是数据显示在当前performance level下selective verification lacks statistical\n    grounding。Paper中可以brief mention作为'future work when base agent is stronger'。\n- name: Selective verification implementation\n  plan_id: plan_006\n  description: 实现binary verify/skip decision。Code-only, no GPU。\n  expected_results:\n    implementation_status: completed\n    code_lines_added: 350\n    integration_test_pass: true\n    note: implementation ready but not deployed for training due to plan_005 results\n  result_rationale: Implementation本身是engineering work，不受worst档影响。代码可以完成，但基于plan_005的统计结果（action-change\n    correlation not significant），decision是不proceed to training。代码保留为future work artifact。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 在worst档叙事下，这个实验stop at implementation。Paper中不报告selective verification\n    training results，而是在discussion section brief mention implementation exists but\n    'requires stronger base agent to provide meaningful training signal'。\n- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Train selective verification policy via episode-level GRPO。在worst档下执行但预期效果不佳。\n  expected_results:\n    training_status: completed_but_ineffective\n    final_success_rate: 18.0\n    always_on_baseline_success: 25.0\n    success_delta_vs_always_on: -7.0\n    verification_rate_reduction: 12.0\n    cost_reduction_pct: 8.0\n    training_stability: unstable\n    convergence_step: no clear convergence\n    reward_signal_noise: high\n  result_rationale: Worst档定义selective_verification_rate_reduction在0-15%，selective_vs_always_on_success_delta在8-15pp。模型从25%\n    base开始，加入verify/skip decision后引入额外exploration space，但base performance本身就marginal。Agent在只有25%\n    success的情况下，缺乏足够的positive reward signal来学习WHEN to verify——大部分trajectory都是failure，无论verify还是skip。结果是verification\n    rate仅下降12%（几乎always verify因为policy没学到有用的skip pattern），且success下降7pp（从25%到18%）因为额外decision\n    point增加了policy complexity。这不构成meaningful contribution。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: B-IAVR training outcome'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Success(%)\n    - Verify Rate(%)\n    - Cost Reduction(%)\n    rows:\n    - - Always-on (baseline)\n      - 25.0\n      - 100\n      - 0\n    - - B-IAVR (trained)\n      - 18.0\n      - 88\n      - 8\n    - - Delta\n      - -7.0\n      - -12\n      - '+8'\n  figures_description:\n  - Training curve extremely noisy, no clear trend in verification rate reduction\n    over steps.\n  analysis: 结果confirms worst档prediction：selective verification在base agent只有25%时无法有意义地训练。-7pp\n    success drop换取仅8% cost reduction，Pareto-dominated by always-on。Paper中不报告此结果，或仅作为negative\n    result brief mention to motivate 'stronger base agent needed'。\n- name: Selective verification full comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Compare always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence-threshold。\n  expected_results:\n    always_on_success: 25.0\n    always_on_verify_rate: 100\n    biavr_success: 18.0\n    biavr_verify_rate: 88\n    no_verify_success: 15.0\n    no_verify_verify_rate: 0\n    random_p50_success: 20.0\n    random_p50_verify_rate: 50\n    confidence_threshold_success: 21.0\n    confidence_threshold_verify_rate: 65\n  result_rationale: 在25% ceiling下，所有selective methods都worse than always-on。Random-p=0.5\n    (20%) actually competitive with trained B-IAVR (18%)——trained policy没有学到比random更好的策略，这是devastating\n    negative result。Confidence-threshold (21%) slightly better因为它是heuristic rule而非learned，less\n    prone to policy degradation。整个comparison suite展示：在low-performance regime下，verification的选择性本身不是bottleneck，base\n    capability才是。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Full comparison (NOT included in worst-tier paper)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Success(%)\n    - Verify Rate(%)\n    - Tokens/Episode\n    - Cost Reduction(%)\n    rows:\n    - - Always-on\n      - 25.0\n      - 100\n      - 4800\n      - 0\n    - - B-IAVR (ours)\n      - 18.0\n      - 88\n      - 4420\n      - 8\n    - - No-verify\n      - 15.0\n      - 0\n      - 2400\n      - 50\n    - - Random-p=0.5\n      - 20.0\n      - 50\n      - 3600\n      - 25\n    - - Confidence-threshold\n      - 21.0\n      - 65\n      - 3900\n      - 19\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Pareto plot (x=cost, y=success): B-IAVR dominated by random-p and confidence-threshold.\n    Only always-on achieves max success.'\n  analysis: 'This entire comparison suite becomes ''data we collected but don''t include\n    in paper''。B-IAVR被simpler baselines dominate是fatal for selective verification\n    claim。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这组数据的唯一价值是supporting the narrative ''future\n    work: once episode-level training achieves higher ceiling, selective verification\n    becomes viable''。'\n- name: No-verify ablation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification。Lower bound实验。\n  expected_results:\n    success_rate: 15.0\n    action_is_valid: 78.0\n    delta_vs_always_on: -10.0\n    mean_episode_length: 38\n    convergence_step: 10\n  result_rationale: 移除verification后，agent失去每步的self-correction机会。从25%降到15%，delta=10pp。这在worst档下actually是有用的数据点——证明verification本身有10pp价值。但这个delta不够dramatic来支撑'selective\n    verification is the key innovation'的story。在pure methodology paper中可以brief report作为：'verification\n    contributes +10pp, confirming its utility, but our focus is on the training methodology\n    that enables ANY multi-turn RL to work'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Verification value'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - Success(%)\n    - Action Valid(%)\n    - Avg Steps\n    rows:\n    - - Episode-level + verification\n      - 25.0\n      - 88.0\n      - 48\n    - - Episode-level, no verification\n      - 15.0\n      - 78.0\n      - 38\n    - - Step-independent + verification\n      - 0.0\n      - 65.0\n      - 50\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '三行对比table实际很有说服力：step-independent完全fails无论有无verification，episode-level\n    without verification仍有15%。Message: training methodology是前提条件，verification是锦上添花。这fit\n    worst档pure methodology paper的narrative。'\n- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Stratify action-change correlation by policy entropy, test partial\n    correlation。\n  expected_results:\n    overall_correlation_r: 0.15\n    overall_p: 0.18\n    low_entropy_stratum_r: 0.08\n    low_entropy_stratum_p: 0.55\n    high_entropy_stratum_r: 0.2\n    high_entropy_stratum_p: 0.22\n    partial_correlation_controlling_entropy: 0.12\n    partial_correlation_p: 0.28\n    n_episodes_per_stratum: 24\n  result_rationale: 在worst档25% success下，整体correlation已not significant (r=0.15, p=0.18)。Stratify\n    by entropy后每层只有~24 episodes，statistical power进一步削弱。Low entropy stratum（policy\n    confident）中action-change很少发生（agent已committed to action），correlation near zero。High\n    entropy stratum中有more action-change但也more randomness，correlation略高但仍not significant。Partial\n    correlation r=0.12 (p=0.28)完全不支持'action-change is signal not noise'的claim。根本原因：样本量太小\n    + base performance太低导致signal-to-noise ratio极差。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '在worst档下这组分析的结论是negative：无法reject null hypothesis (action-change = noise)。Paper中不report，或在appendix作为''limitation:\n    at current performance level, insufficient statistical power to establish action-change\n    as reliable signal''。'\n- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered. Compare success。\n  expected_results:\n    verification_triggered_success: 22.0\n    random_change_success: 16.0\n    no_change_baseline_success: 18.0\n    delta_triggered_vs_random: 6.0\n    delta_triggered_vs_random_p: 0.25\n    n_episodes: 48\n  result_rationale: Verification-triggered changes (22%) vs random changes (16%) shows\n    6pp gap，方向正确但p=0.25 not significant。N=48 episodes不够detect这个effect size。No-change\n    baseline (18%)介于两者之间，使得interpretation模糊：triggered changes可能beneficial，但也可能just\n    noise given wide CIs。在25% performance regime下，即使verification IS informative，effect\n    size太小to detect reliably。另一个confounder：random changes有时accidentally correct（16%\n    vs no-change 18%只差2pp），suggesting verification的causal contribution marginal。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Causal intervention (insufficient power)'\n    columns:\n    - Condition\n    - Success(%)\n    - N\n    - 95% CI\n    rows:\n    - - Verification-triggered change\n      - 22.0\n      - 48\n      - '[11%, 33%]'\n    - - Random change (same rate)\n      - 16.0\n      - 48\n      - '[6%, 26%]'\n    - - No change control\n      - 18.0\n      - 48\n      - '[8%, 28%]'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: CIs完全overlap。Experiment was run but results inconclusive。在pure methodology\n    paper中不report。File under 'more data needed at higher performance level'。\n- name: Reward signal ablation (action-change vs alternatives)\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: 'Train B-IAVR with different reward signals: action-change, random,\n    confidence-based。'\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_reward_success: 18.0\n    action_change_reward_verify_rate: 88\n    random_reward_success: 17.0\n    random_reward_verify_rate: 82\n    confidence_reward_success: 19.0\n    confidence_reward_verify_rate: 85\n    all_configs_worse_than_always_on: true\n    best_reward_signal: confidence (marginal)\n  result_rationale: 所有reward signals在25% base下都无法学到meaningful selective policy。Action-change\n    reward (18%, verify 88%) vs random reward (17%, verify 82%)的差距仅1pp success——action-change没有demonstrable\n    advantage over random。Confidence-based reward margionally better (19%) because它at\n    least correlates with model's own uncertainty（哪怕calibration差）。但关键point：所有trained\n    selective policies都worse than always-on (25%)。Reward signal choice irrelevant\n    when base performance insufficient to generate learning signal。192 GPU hours换来的结论是'all\n    approaches fail equally in low-performance regime'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Reward ablation (NOT in paper)'\n    columns:\n    - Reward Signal\n    - Success(%)\n    - Verify Rate(%)\n    - vs Always-on Delta\n    rows:\n    - - Action-change (ours)\n      - 18.0\n      - 88\n      - -7\n    - - Random trigger\n      - 17.0\n      - 82\n      - -8\n    - - Confidence-based\n      - 19.0\n      - 85\n      - -6\n    - - Always-on (no selection)\n      - 25.0\n      - 100\n      - 0\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 192 GPU hours for a negative result。在worst档下，建议NOT run此实验——plan_007的negative\n    result已sufficient to abandon selective verification direction。Save GPU budget\n    for more h-sweep seeds or ScienceWorld transfer。\n- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR。\n  expected_results:\n    ares_success: 20.0\n    ares_verify_rate: 60\n    ares_cost_reduction: 30\n    biavr_success: 18.0\n    biavr_verify_rate: 88\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 8\n    ares_dominates_biavr: true\n  result_rationale: ARES使用SFT（supervised从expert demonstrations学）which is more data-efficient\n    than RL in low-performance regime。SFT router可以直接学human-pattern的'when to verify'而不依赖agent自身的exploration。预测ARES\n    achieves 20% success at 60% verify rate，Pareto-dominating B-IAVR (18% at 88% verify\n    rate)。这是because SFT不需要agent自己产生positive signal——它从expert data中学。Devastating for\n    our RL-based approach，但irrelevant for worst档paper because we abandon selective\n    verification entirely。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: ARES comparison (NOT in paper)'\n    columns:\n    - Method\n    - Success(%)\n    - Verify Rate(%)\n    - Cost Red.(%)\n    rows:\n    - - Always-on\n      - 25.0\n      - 100\n      - 0\n    - - ARES (SFT router)\n      - 20.0\n      - 60\n      - 30\n    - - B-IAVR (ours, RL)\n      - 18.0\n      - 88\n      - 8\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: ARES dominates B-IAVR on Pareto frontier。但在worst档pure methodology paper中，这个comparison不needed也不helpful。如果include，只会invite\n    reviewer质疑'why not just use SFT'。建议NOT run，节省24 GPU hours。\n- name: ScienceWorld transfer (episode-level advantage)\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld。Second environment\n    for generalization。\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_success: 15.0\n    step_independent_success: 2.0\n    episode_level_action_is_valid: 75.0\n    step_independent_action_is_valid: 55.0\n    episode_level_convergence_step: 12\n    step_independent_collapse_step: 4\n    mean_episode_length_scienceworld: 35\n  result_rationale: ScienceWorld比ALFWorld更难（state space更大，natural language更复杂），1.7B\n    model的absolute performance会更低。Episode-level仍展示优势（15% vs 2%），倍率~7.5x（高于ALFWorld的~4x因为ScienceWorld的longer\n    episodes使credit assignment问题更severe）。Step-independent在step 4 collapse（与ALFWorld\n    pattern一致）。绝对数字15%不impressive，但cross-environment consistency是powerful evidence\n    for the mechanism。在worst档pure methodology paper中，这是ADDRESS single-environment\n    concern的关键实验。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-environment validation'\n    columns:\n    - Environment\n    - Episode-Level(%)\n    - Step-Independent(%)\n    - Ratio\n    - Mean Episode Length\n    rows:\n    - - ALFWorld\n      - 25.0\n      - 0.0\n      - ∞ (0→25)\n      - 48\n    - - ScienceWorld\n      - 15.0\n      - 2.0\n      - 7.5x\n      - 35\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Side-by-side training curves for both environments. Same pattern: step-independent\n    collapses early, episode-level converges (albeit to low absolute value).'\n  analysis: 'Cross-environment result是worst档paper的第二大contribution。Pattern consistent\n    across environments strongly支持mechanistic explanation。Reviewer concern #2 (single\n    env) addressed。72 GPU hours well-spent for worst档narrative。绝对值低但ratio large，且collapse\n    pattern identical——这是methodology insight的generalization evidence。'\n- name: 7B model scaling verification\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B。Address model size concern。\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_7b_success: 38.0\n    step_independent_7b_success: 5.0\n    episode_level_7b_action_is_valid: 92.0\n    step_independent_7b_collapse_step: 5\n    episode_level_7b_convergence_step: 6\n    delta_7b_vs_1_7b_episode_level: 13\n  result_rationale: 7B model有更高的capability ceiling，episode-level可能达38%（接近40% threshold但仍在worst档范围内——worst档是关于1.7B的performance，7B\n    naturally higher）。Step-independent 7B同样collapse at step 5 (5% max)，确认credit assignment问题is\n    model-size independent。7B的38% vs 1.7B的25%（+13pp）部分validates 'model capacity is\n    separate bottleneck' argument。但192 GPU hours + cloud rental成本高。在worst档下，如果budget\n    tight，这是high-value但high-cost experiment。如果run，结果强力支持narrative：'episode-level advantage\n    holds across scales; larger models achieve higher ceiling但step-independent依然fails\n    regardless of scale'。\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Model scaling'\n    columns:\n    - Model\n    - Episode-Level(%)\n    - Step-Independent(%)\n    - Advantage\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - 25.0\n      - 0.0\n      - +25pp\n    - - Qwen3-7B\n      - 38.0\n      - 5.0\n      - +33pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: episode-level advantage grows with model size (from +25pp to +33pp),\n    suggesting larger models benefit MORE from episode-level training (because they\n    have more capacity to exploit the better gradient signal).'\n  analysis: '如果budget允许，这是worst档paper最能silence reviewer的实验。7B result (38% vs 5%) is\n    more impressive than 1.7B result (25% vs 0%)。Combined message: ''the training\n    methodology enables the model capacity to be utilized; without it, even larger\n    models fail''。论文可能需要重新定位：如果7B reaches 38%，接近40% threshold，paper的overall strength\n    significantly improves even under worst-tier 1.7B results。'\n- name: Per-task-type breakdown analysis\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: Breakdown by ALFWorld task type. Shows within-environment diversity。\n  expected_results:\n    pick_success_episode_level: 30.0\n    pick_success_step_independent: 0.0\n    clean_success_episode_level: 20.0\n    clean_success_step_independent: 0.0\n    heat_success_episode_level: 25.0\n    heat_success_step_independent: 0.0\n    cool_success_episode_level: 35.0\n    cool_success_step_independent: 5.0\n    examine_success_episode_level: 10.0\n    examine_success_step_independent: 0.0\n    pick_two_success_episode_level: 5.0\n    pick_two_success_step_independent: 0.0\n    episode_length_success_correlation: -0.42\n    short_task_advantage: cool/heat (fewer steps) have higher success\n  result_rationale: '在worst档下，per-task breakdown reveals episode-level advantage is\n    universal但magnitude varies by task complexity。Shorter tasks (cool: ~30 steps,\n    heat: ~35 steps) reach higher success (35%, 25%) because credit assignment even\n    under h=full works better when T is smaller (gamma^0=1 for last step matters more\n    when T smaller)。Longer tasks (examine: ~50 steps, pick_two: ~55 steps) have lower\n    success (10%, 5%) — model capacity ceiling hits harder when trajectory is longer。Correlation\n    r=-0.42 between episode length and success confirms mechanistic explanation。Step-independent\n    fails uniformly across all types (0-5%), confirming the training failure is systematic\n    not task-specific。'\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Per-task breakdown'\n    columns:\n    - Task Type\n    - Avg Episode Length\n    - Episode-Level(%)\n    - Step-Independent(%)\n    - N (val)\n    rows:\n    - - pick\n      - 45\n      - 30.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 4\n    - - clean\n      - 48\n      - 20.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 3\n    - - heat\n      - 35\n      - 25.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 3\n    - - cool\n      - 30\n      - 35.0\n      - 5.0\n      - 3\n    - - examine\n      - 50\n      - 10.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 2\n    - - pick_two\n      - 55\n      - 5.0\n      - 0.0\n      - 1\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Scatter plot: x=mean episode length per task type, y=episode-level success rate.\n    Negative correlation visible. Annotation: ''longer tasks → weaker signal even\n    with full context (more steps to credit-assign across)''.'\n  analysis: Small N per task type (1-4 episodes in val set) makes individual percentages\n    unreliable，但overall trend (shorter tasks → higher success) supports mechanistic\n    story。In worst档paper，include as supplementary analysis showing the method's advantage\n    is consistent across task types despite varying magnitude。The length-success correlation\n    adds another data point for the credit assignment narrative。\n","numLines":740,"startLine":1,"totalLines":740}}}
