{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013i12vM2AUJRYyhwHB8ngyP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dszu7SQMtyAqL7dLYC6tXn","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__director_post_to_reviewer","input":{"text":"[Dream 审稿任务 — Reviewer 1：方法 + 实验]\n\n论文标题：Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Training Fails and How to Fix It\n\n论文摘要：本文识别了 step-independent reward assignment 在 multi-turn agent RL 训练中的根本失败模式——credit assignment decay（γ^(T-h) → 0），提出 episode-level GRPO 作为解决方案。在 ALFWorld 和 ScienceWorld 上用 Qwen3-1.7B 实验，episode-level 训练达到 24.3%±6.0% success vs step-independent 的 0%。h-sweep 揭示 h<5 时存在 sharp cliff。优势泛化到 ScienceWorld (15% vs 2%) 和 Qwen3-7B (38% vs 5%)。\n\n论文结构概览（8页）：\n- §1 Introduction：识别 credit assignment decay 问题，提出 episode-level GRPO\n- §2 Related Work：RL for LM agents、multi-turn frameworks、credit assignment in RL、adaptive computation\n- §3 Method：问题公式化（Eq.1 gradient signal decay）、credit assignment decay analysis（Eq.2）、episode-level GRPO（Eq.3）\n- §4 Experiments：\n  - 4.1 Setup：ALFWorld (T=48)、ScienceWorld (T=35)、Qwen3-1.7B/7B、GRPO with KL=0.01, G=8, lr=5e-6\n  - 4.2 Context Window Sweep (Table 1)：h∈{1,2,3,5,8,10,15,20,full}，h≤2 collapse，h<5 sharp cliff\n  - 4.3 Multi-Seed (Table 2)：3 seeds，24.3%±6.0%\n  - 4.4 Credit Assignment Mechanism (Table 3)：γ^(T-h) vs observed success correlation\n  - 4.5 Verification Value (Table 4)：episode-level+verify 25%, no-verify 15%, step-indep+verify 0%\n  - 4.6 Cross-Environment (Table 5)：ALFWorld 25/0, ScienceWorld 15/2\n  - 4.7 Model Scale (Table 6)：1.7B 25/0, 7B 38/5\n  - 4.8 Per-Task Breakdown (Table 7)：6 task types, r=-0.42 correlation with episode length\n- §5 Discussion：relationship to RAGEN, model capacity bottleneck, practical guidance, limitations, future work\n- §6 Conclusion\n- References：10 entries\n\n实验设计参考（review_context.yaml 中的完整实验列表）：\n共 16 个 imagined experiments：\n1. h-sweep (plan_002) — 已在 Table 1 报告\n2. Multi-seed 3 seeds (plan_003) — 已在 Table 2 报告\n3. Credit assignment mechanism analysis (plan_004) — 已在 Table 3 报告\n4. Action-change statistics (plan_005) — 论文未报告（统计不显著）\n5. Selective verification implementation (plan_006) — 代码完成但未训练\n6. B-IAVR selective verification training (plan_007) — 训练完成但效果差（success 从25%降到18%），论文未报告\n7. Selective verification full comparison (plan_008) — 5种方法对比，B-IAVR被simpler baselines dominate，论文未报告\n8. Full comparison (plan_008) — 论文未报告\n9. No-verify ablation (plan_009) — 已在 Table 4 报告\n10. Entropy-controlled analysis (plan_010) — 结果negative，论文未报告\n11. Causal intervention (plan_011) — 结果inconclusive (p=0.25)，论文未报告\n12. Reward signal ablation (plan_012) — 所有方法都worse than always-on，论文未报告\n13. ARES reproduction (plan_013) — ARES dominates B-IAVR，论文未报告\n14. ScienceWorld transfer (plan_014) — 已在 Table 5 报告\n15. 7B scaling (plan_015) — 已在 Table 6 报告\n16. Per-task breakdown (plan_016) — 已在 Table 7 报告\n\n你的审查侧重：\n- **方法描述**：是否完整、claim 是否被实验数据支撑、关键超参/训练流程是否清晰\n- **实验设计**：是否覆盖关键 baseline/ablation/跨数据集/scale 维度\n- **数据呈现**：表格/图是否能让审稿人复现结论、误差棒/统计显著性是否充分\n\n具体关注点：\n1. Eq.1 中的 gradient signal decay 公式是否严谨——GRPO 是否真的使用 γ discount？还是论文将 credit assignment 问题框架化为 discount decay 只是一个类比？\n2. h-sweep 只有 single seed（除 h=full 有 3 seeds）——中间 h 值的 ordering 是否可靠？\n3. 24.3%±6.0% 的绝对性能——3 seeds 的 95% CI 极宽（约 [12%, 37%]），统计power是否足够支撑 claims？\n4. 论文放弃了 selective verification 方向但未报告 negative results——这是否构成 incomplete reporting？\n5. ScienceWorld 和 7B 实验是否也只有 single seed？如果是，跨环境/跨scale 的 claims 基础薄弱\n6. Per-task breakdown N=1-4，统计意义存疑\n7. 论文只对比 step-independent baseline，缺少与其他 credit assignment 方法（如 eligibility traces、GAE、hindsight relabeling）的对比\n\n请基于论文内容独立评判，不要假设论文结果的质量高低。\n\n**不要评判**：新颖性/相关工作（那是 Reviewer 2 的范围）、格式/排版。\n\n请通过 `review_reviewer_post_to_director(text, reviewer_id=\"1\", project=\"cost-verify-agent-rl\", dream_id=\"20260516T235255\")` 汇报。","reviewer_id":"1","project":"cost-verify-agent-rl","round_number":1},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1594,"cache_read_input_tokens":57481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1594},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6de2f966-8909-4f3c-95c6-636800eb7308","uuid":"7082e0e2-f331-44f3-b6fa-dac1f4f0f6fa"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dszu7SQMtyAqL7dLYC6tXn","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"reviewer_key\\\": \\\"feishu:group:oc_648eaf83d2b24d445764257cf6a55525:reviewer_1\\\"}, \\\"error\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6de2f966-8909-4f3c-95c6-636800eb7308","uuid":"a8db28a5-b34c-4e6a-8d18-4d75d182844d","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:27:54.896Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"reviewer_key\\\": \\\"feishu:group:oc_648eaf83d2b24d445764257cf6a55525:reviewer_1\\\"}, \\\"error\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"}","structuredContent":{"result":"{\"success\": true, \"data\": {\"reviewer_key\": \"feishu:group:oc_648eaf83d2b24d445764257cf6a55525:reviewer_1\"}, \"error\": \"\"}"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_013i12vM2AUJRYyhwHB8ngyP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HrMZVEQeHM1aRtLbi8RTMT","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__director_post_to_reviewer","input":{"text":"[Dream 审稿任务 — Reviewer 2：新颖性 + 相关工作]\n\n论文标题：Episode-Level RL for Multi-Turn Agents: Why Step-Independent Training Fails and How to Fix It\n\n论文摘要：本文识别了 step-independent reward assignment 在 multi-turn agent RL 训练中的根本失败模式——credit assignment decay（γ^(T-h) → 0），提出 episode-level GRPO 作为解决方案。在 ALFWorld 和 ScienceWorld 上用 Qwen3-1.7B 实验，episode-level 训练达到 24.3%±6.0% success vs step-independent 的 0%。h-sweep 揭示 h<5 时存在 sharp cliff。优势泛化到 ScienceWorld (15% vs 2%) 和 Qwen3-7B (38% vs 5%)。\n\n论文结构概览（8页）：\n- §1 Introduction：4 contributions listed — (1) identify credit assignment decay, (2) episode-level GRPO achieves 24.3%, (3) h-sweep with cliff at h=5, (4) cross-env and cross-scale validation\n- §2 Related Work：4 paragraphs covering RL for LM agents (RAGEN, AgentQ), multi-turn frameworks (Self-Guide 72.7%, ReflAct, ARES), credit assignment in RL (TD, eligibility traces, HER), adaptive computation (Thinkless)\n- §3 Method：problem formulation, credit assignment decay analysis (γ^(T-h)), episode-level GRPO (Eq.3)\n- §4 Experiments：7 tables covering h-sweep, multi-seed, mechanism analysis, verification ablation, cross-env, model scale, per-task breakdown\n- §5 Discussion：relationship to RAGEN, model capacity as separate bottleneck, practical guidance, limitations, future directions\n- §6 Conclusion\n- References：10 entries total — [1] RAGEN 2025, [2] Self-Guide 2026, [3] ARES 2026, [4] Thinkless NeurIPS 2025, [5] ReflAct EMNLP 2025, [6] ALFWorld ICLR 2021, [7] ScienceWorld EMNLP 2022, [8] DeepSeekMath 2024, [9] Qwen 2024, [10] Sutton & Barto 2018\n\n实验设计参考（review_context.yaml）：\n论文原本计划 16 个实验，但最终放弃了 selective verification 方向的多个实验（plan_005 到 plan_013 中大部分），因为统计结果不支持。论文叙事从 \"selective verification\" 转型为 \"pure training methodology\"。\n\n你的审查侧重：\n- **新颖性**：与现有工作的差异化是否清晰、贡献点是否独立成立\n- **相关工作**：文献覆盖是否充分、重要 baseline 是否漏引、定位是否准确\n- **Story 一致性**：论证逻辑是否自洽（intro/abstract/conclusion 的 claim 不能与 method/experiments 矛盾）\n\n具体关注点：\n1. 核心贡献是 \"use full episode context for GRPO training\" —— 这是否足够构成一篇顶会论文的 novelty？episode-level reward assignment 在传统 RL 中是 default，论文是否充分论证了为什么这在 LLM agent RL 中被遗忘/忽略？\n2. Related Work 只有 10 references，对于 top ML venue 显著偏少。关键缺失：\n   - AgentQ 只提名字未给引用\n   - 没有引用 PPO/REINFORCE 等基础 RL 算法\n   - 没有引用 GAE (Generalized Advantage Estimation) 这个直接相关的 credit assignment 方法\n   - 没有引用 hindsight experience replay (HER) 的具体论文\n   - 没有引用其他 multi-turn LLM agent training 工作（如 WebAgent、AgentTuning、FireAct 等）\n3. Self-Guide 达到 72.7% on ALFWorld with Qwen-1.7B，而本文 episode-level 只有 25%——论文如何 position 自己？Discussion 中提到 \"model capacity is separate bottleneck\" 但 Self-Guide 用同样大小的模型达到了远高的性能\n4. 论文 claim \"identify credit assignment decay as root cause\" 但 γ^(T-h) decay 是基础 RL 教科书内容——novelty 是否仅在于 \"指出 RAGEN 的默认配置有问题\"？\n5. Story 一致性：Introduction 说 \"episode-level GRPO eliminates this bottleneck\"，但 25% success 表明还有其他 major bottlenecks——claim 是否 overclaimed？\n6. Future directions 提到 selective verification 需要 >40% base agent——这暗示当前工作是一个 stepping stone 而非 standalone contribution\n\n请基于论文内容独立评判，不要假设论文结果的质量高低。\n\n**不要评判**：方法实现细节/实验设计（那是 Reviewer 1 的范围）、格式/排版。\n\n请通过 `review_reviewer_post_to_director(text, reviewer_id=\"2\", project=\"cost-verify-agent-rl\", dream_id=\"20260516T235255\")` 汇报。","reviewer_id":"2","project":"cost-verify-agent-rl","round_number":1},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1594,"cache_read_input_tokens":57481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1594},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6de2f966-8909-4f3c-95c6-636800eb7308","uuid":"b0bd44b1-a841-4d4c-b492-594877dcdc51"}
